# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# TRIVY IGNORE FILE — Acknowledged CVE Suppressions
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This file documents CVEs that have been reviewed by the team and
# are temporarily suppressed because:
#   (a) No fix is available yet in the upstream Spring Boot / Tomcat
#       release line compatible with our current stack, OR
#   (b) The CVE does not affect the code paths used by this app.
#
# IMPORTANT: This is NOT "ignoring security". This is the standard
# industry practice of acknowledging known, reviewed risks while
# keeping the gate active for NEW unknown CVEs.
#
# Each entry must have a documented reason. Review this file every
# sprint and remove entries when fixes become available.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

